        <p>_ Ile •ar heartily *thankt,d the workers for u 'ping him.to organise another sale of work, itilu,sPite of many difficulties. It was a good Lung, he said, that they had something to do out Side the war. If they werElThlways thinking .4,bout the war, it was bound to do them harm.r, 4lthouh they should think about if a great deal t' 4.L. hey should not let it have all their e"loughts. He trusted that the sale would be a nilecess, because- money was wanted. for the Qiurch Extension Fund, the Endowment Fund, hOd the Curacy Fund, and he hoped that the teault of the sale would be that they would be to give something to each of those funds. ;Ihey were very pleased to have \Mrs. Parr With them. She had, undoubtedly; opened more sales of work than anyone else in Warrington.</p>
