      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-05-22_WidnesExaminer_art0301" n="art0301">
        <head>TO-DAY'S TOURNEYS.</head>
        <p>TO-DAY'S TOURNEYS.</p>
        <p>The games arranged for to-day are four 'in number, and they will be refereed by Mr. J. Willett. These games stand postponed from April 24th—when the weather was so wet that play was practically impossible—and the con- testing teams will be:- 2 pan.: Armitage and Rigby's v. Walker's No. 2. 2.45 p.m.: Pearson and Knowles' Engineers v. Howley' Tannery. 3.30 p. 111.: Warrington Tannery v. Monks, Hall's. 4.15 p.m.: Mersey White Lead v. Pearson and Knowles' (Bewsey).</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-05-22_WidnesExaminer_art0302" n="art0302">
        <head>COUNTY AMATEUR BOWLING</head>
        <p>COUNTY AMATEUR BOWLING</p>
        <p>ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>One Local Team Left In.</p>
        <p>BULL'S HEAD STILL GOING STRONG.</p>
        <p>, The Bull's Head, Warrington, team have suc- cessfully weathered the second round of the Lancashire Club Championship, beatieg the Prestwich Conservatives by the fairly com- fortable total of 24. The match was played at Flixton on Saturday, and produced some pretty bowling, as well as some that was fairly in- different, the Warrington men, on the whole, thoroughly deserving their win. The individual scores were : _ . . _</p>
        <p>Bull's Head. F. Casey W. H. Eyes George Shaw T. Hackett . .. A. Regan . ..... A. Gleave (No. 2) J. Isherwood E. Shaw ...... A. Randles W. ,Milman- W. Skelhome J. W. Plinston</p>
