      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-05-22_WidnesExaminer_art0304" n="art0304">
        <head>ASSOCIATION COMPETITION.</head>
        <p>ASSOCIATION COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>Draw for the First Round.</p>
        <p>At a meeting of. the Lancashire County Bowling Association, held at Manchester on Monday, the draw for the first round of the association competition, to take place to-day, was made as follows :</p>
        <p>Middleton Old Cock v. Warrington Cemetery, at Chorlton Bowling Green. Ship 11qtel, Irlam, v. Earlestown, at the Bull's H:ead, Warrington. . .</p>
        <p>Midway v. Promenade, Southport, at War- rington Cemetery. Trafford Hotel v. Peel Green, at Weaste Con- servative Club.</p>
        <p>Whitefield v. George, Prestwich, at Red Lion, Prestwich. Kersal v. Heaton Park Conservatives, at Prestwich Liberal. Weaste Conservatives v. Red Lion, Prestwich, at Griffin, Lower Broughton. Prestwich Conservatives v. Stretford Angel, -at the George, Prestwich. Irlams-o'-th'-Height Conservatives v. Radcliffe Withens, at Prestwich Conservative. Eccles Oddfellows v. Denton, at Cheetham Temple. Cheetham Temple v. Pendleton Belmont, at Whitefield. Sandon, Lixerpool, v. Bedford Conservative, at Newton-le-Willows. Leigh Railway v. Lord Nelson, at Eccles Oddfellows.</p>
        <p>Griffin v. Wigan Limited, at Urmston Vic- toria. "</p>
        <p>C.W.S., Irlam, v. Leigh Liberals, at Kersal Hotel.</p>
        <p>Prestwich Liberals v. chorlton, at Stretford Angel.</p>
        <p>Second Team Championship.</p>
        <p>The draw for the second round a the second team competition was made as follows</p>
        <p>Kersal v. Warrington Cemetery, at Roebuck, Ilixton.</p>
        <p>Lord Nelson v. Newton-le-Willows, at Elles- mere Hotel, Leigh.</p>
