        <p>Consolation.</p>
        <p>The second teams' consolation competitiafi draw resulted :</p>
        <p>Pendleton Belmont v. Irlams-o'-th'-Height Conservatives, at Radcliffe Withens. The remainder of the clubs were given byes</p>
        <p>Mid-week Competition.</p>
        <p>It was decided to arrange the mid-week com- petition in four sections, clubs .to play home- and-home matches, results to be decided on aggregate points, the district champions to play off for the competition championship. The sections arranged were No. 1 Section.—Warrington Bull's Head, New- ton-le-Willows; Royal Excelsior, and Rainhill. No. 2 Section.—lrlams-o'-th'-Height Conser- vatives; Weaste Conservatives, Griffin (Lower Broughton), and Pendleton Belmont. No. 3 Section.—C.W.S. (Irlam), Roebuck, Midway, and Urmston Victoria. No. 4 Section.—Ber,sal, Prestwich 'ConserVa- lives, Radcliffe Withens, and George (Prest- wich).</p>
      </div>
