        <p>Additional Names.</p>
        <p>Last week we published a roll of honour compiled by Mr. E. A. Sanders, Liberal Agent, consisting of Liberal ward workers and sons and brothers of ward workers who have joined the forces. The list was necessarily incomplete. Additions and corrections were ahked for, and during the past week the following have come to 'hand. Mr. Sanders will be pleased to have further names for the list, which will eventu- ally be placed either in the Club or in the John Crosfield Memorial Hall, and additions should be forwarded at the earliest possible moment, so that the roll may be framed and hung. The additions are as follow :</p>
        <p>ADDITHYNAL NAMES.—First List.</p>
        <p>TOWN HALL WARD. Gibson, John Kenwright, 6th Cheshire Regt Gibson, Wm. P., 2/ 4th Smith Lanes. Gibson, James, King's Royal-Rifles. Gibson, Ernest George, A.S.C.</p>
