        <p>DIED OF WOUNDS. SECOND-LIEUT. IVAN FULTON-SM ITH. A Good Officer Who Was Promoted From Sergeant. News was received yesterday by Mr. J. Fulton-Smith, of 20, Bold-street, Warrington, that his son, Second-Lieutenant Ivan Fulton- Smith of the 9th Royal Scots Regiment, had died in hospital on the 20th May. The intimation came in the form of a telegraphic message, merely stating that the gallant officer had died as the result of a wound received on the 23rd or 24th April. He was a widower.</p>
